id: boomerang
name: Boomerang
kind: crafting
types: physical
slots: 1~2
requiresQualities: throwing-weapon
excludesQualities: multi-storage
prerequisites: Throwing Weapon Weapon Quality, you do not have the Multi-Storage Weapon Quality.
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Thrown, it may be taken in hand again at once. With 2 Slots, the Homing Advantage on the
  throw.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: If you throw this Weapon through the Throw Maneuver, you may equip it again
  immediately, ignoring the distance between you and the Weapon.

  [Passive]: If this Weapon Quality takes up 2 Slots, apply the Homing Advantage to any
  Attacking Maneuver made with this Weapon through the Throw Maneuver.
text: >
  Boomerang: This Weapon returns to your hand after you throw it.
  –Weapon Type: Physical
  –Prerequisites: Throwing Weapon Weapon Quality, you do not have the Multi-Storage Weapon
  Quality.
  –Quality Slots: 1~2
  –Effects: If you throw this Weapon through the Throw Maneuver, you may equip it again
  immediately, ignoring the distance between you and the Weapon.

  If this Weapon Quality takes up 2 Slots, apply the Homing Advantage to any Attacking Maneuver
  made with this Weapon through the Throw Maneuver.

---

# Thrown from the hand, it is asked whether it comes back into it; otherwise it is out of hand, as
# any thrown Weapon is.
[passive]
weapon.returns += $slots;

# --- What is not built ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Homing Advantage is not in this system. With 2 Slots the throw has it, and what it does is
# the table's until it is.
